{"id":"lcss_distance","title":"One minus LCSS similarity","family":"elastic","definition":"echotime","intro_en":"This distance-like transform is one minus the normalized LCSS match count. It retains the order-preserving, tolerance-based matching rule. The final conversion reverses the direction of the score without restoring information discarded by skipped points or thresholding; different sequences can therefore receive zero distance.","intro_zh":"该距离形式等于一减归一化 LCSS 匹配数量，仍采用保持顺序的容差匹配。最后的变换只反转分数方向，无法恢复跳过观测或阈值判断丢失的信息，因此不同序列也可能得到零距离。","steps_en":["Set the stated local scoring rule, tolerance and boundary conditions.","Count tolerance matches and carry forward the larger match count when skipping.","Trace the selected predecessor operations from the complete-prefix state.","Convert the count to one minus its shorter-length-normalized value."],"steps_zh":["设置明确的局部计分规则、容差与边界条件。","累计容差内匹配，跳过观测时保留较大的匹配计数。","从完整前缀状态沿选定的前驱操作回溯。","将匹配数量除以较短长度，再用一减去该比例。"],"formula":"d_LCSS=1-LCSS_epsilon(x,y)/min(n,m)","caveats_en":["One minus a similarity need not satisfy metric axioms. Zero here means full tolerance-based coverage of the shorter sequence.","The small arrays are an algorithm illustration, not evidence of retrieval or classification quality."],"caveats_zh":["一减相似度不保证满足度量公理；这里的零值表示较短序列在容差内被完全覆盖。","这些小数组用于解释计算过程，不构成检索或分类性能证据。"],"sources":[{"label":"tslearn: Longest Common Subsequence","url":"https://tslearn.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user_guide/lcss.html"},{"label":"EchoTime low-level similarity implementations","url":"https://github.com/ZipengWu365/EchoTime/blob/main/src/echotime/similarity_methods.py"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"normalization":"match count / min(n,m)","local_norm":"absolute difference","epsilon":0.35},"result":{"label":"distance","value":0.09999999999999998,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown 